      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "Gaho — 시작",
      "content": "Time sequencing. \"Before you leave.\"\n\n시작 means 'beginning' or 'start.' It's the OST for Itaewon Class (이태원 클라쓰), a 2020 Korean drama where the main character, Park Saeroyi, watches his father get killed, gets expelled from school, and goes to prison — all before he's 20. When he gets out, he opens a tiny bar in Itaewon and spends years building it up to take down the conglomerate that destroyed his family.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-기 전에**, which means \"before doing.\" We'll see how Gaho uses it in \"시작.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **시작하다** — to start\n- **끝나다** — to end\n- **떠나기 전에** — before leaving\n- **시작하기 전에** — before starting\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
